ts","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: the healthy pre-restart boot identity was captured, restart was acknowledged and observed through temporary connection loss, the post-restart identity changed, and crond, configuration, executable, retained log data, and output generation recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity transition.","limitations":["No naturally scheduler-triggered 02:15 execution was observed; the conclusion relies on the exact cron configuration, active/enabled scheduler, and successful direct execution through the configured command and log behavior.","The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the installed cron file, script, or log directly; their final state is established by executor commands instead.","Restart recovery evidence is strong for this single-node task, but there was no separate cluster state to assess."]}
